module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalFunctions.AdicGradedPieceShortExact
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Coherent.HomColimit.IdealPowTensorSmul
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Modules.Generators.TensorGloballyGenerated
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorPresentations

/-!
# The graded pieces of the `𝓘`-adic filtration are generated by global sections

Let `X` be a scheme, `𝓘` a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals on it and `M` a quasi-coherent sheaf of
modules. This file produces the surjection

`𝓘 ⁿ ⊗_{𝒪_X} (M / 𝓘 M) ⟶ 𝓘 ⁿ M / 𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹ M`

and deduces that the graded piece `𝓘 ⁿ M / 𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹ M` of the `𝓘`-adic filtration is generated by
global sections as soon as `𝓘 ⁿ` and `M / 𝓘 M` are. This is step (b) of the proof of
[Stacks, Tag 0EXD]: the graded pieces live on the exceptional divisor, where global generation is
what makes their `H¹` vanish, which is the hypothesis
`Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.surjective_adicCohomologyProj_of_isZero_gradedPiece` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalFunctions/AdicGradedPieceShortExact.lean` consumes.

The graded piece is the same object as there, namely
`cokernel (Stacks.Algebraization.submoduleInclusion (idealPowerMultiple_antitone 𝓘 M …))`,
abbreviated `adicGradedPieceModule` below.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Abelian.exactDesc`: the map out of the right-hand term of an exact pair whose second
  map is an epimorphism, with the pair, its vanishing composite and the epimorphism hypothesis
  all presented as variables.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.idealPowIdealTensorToSucc`: the factorization
  `𝓘 ⁿ ⊗ 𝓘 M ⟶ 𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹ M` of multiplication of sections — the mathematical content of the whole
  file.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.idealPowTensorQuotientToGradedPiece`: **the surjection
  `𝓘 ⁿ ⊗_{𝒪_X} (M / 𝓘 M) ⟶ 𝓘 ⁿ M / 𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹ M`.**

## Main results

* `Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.algebraization_idealPowerMultiple_eq`: the two `𝓘 ⁿ M`
  constants of the tree are definitionally equal.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.idealPowTensorIdeal_comp_toGradedPiece`: **the composite
  `𝓘 ⁿ ⊗ 𝓘 M ⟶ 𝓘 ⁿ ⊗ M ⟶ 𝓘 ⁿ M / 𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹ M` is zero**, because `a ⊗ b m ↦ a b m` lands in
  `𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹ M`.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.epi_idealPowTensorQuotientToGradedPiece`: the surjection is
  an epimorphism.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.generatingSectionsAdicGradedPiece`: **the graded piece
  `𝓘 ⁿ M / 𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹ M` is generated by global sections** when `𝓘 ⁿ` and `M / 𝓘 M` are.

## Implementation notes

**The source of the surjection tensors the un-quotiented `𝓘 ⁿ`.** [Stacks, Tag 0EXD] writes the
surjection out of `(𝓘 ⁿ / 𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹) ⊗_{𝒪_E} (M / 𝓘 M)`. Nothing in the use made of it needs the
left factor quotiented: a module is generated by global sections as soon as it receives an
epimorphism from one that is, and `𝓘 ⁿ` is globally generated exactly when `𝓘 ⁿ / 𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹` is in
the situation of the tag. Tensoring `𝓘 ⁿ` itself avoids constructing `𝓘 ⁿ / 𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹` as a sheaf of
modules on the exceptional divisor and pulling the tensor product back to `E`, so that is what is
done here.

**The zero composite is the only mathematics.** `𝓘 ⁿ ⊗ M ⟶ 𝓘 ⁿ M` is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerColimit.idealPowTensorToSmul`, an epimorphism for
quasi-coherent `M`; composing it with the projection onto the graded piece gives an epimorphism
`𝓘 ⁿ ⊗ M ⟶ 𝓘 ⁿ M / 𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹ M`, and everything else is the universal property of a cokernel. What
has to be proved is that `𝓘 ⁿ ⊗ 𝓘 M ⟶ 𝓘 ⁿ ⊗ M ⟶ 𝓘 ⁿ M` factors through `𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹ M`. That is
checked on an affine open around each point, where a section of the tensor product is a finite
sum of pure tensors `∑ aⱼ ⊗ bⱼ` with `aⱼ ∈ 𝓘(V) ⁿ` and `bⱼ ∈ 𝓘(V) Γ(M, V)`, so that each
`aⱼ bⱼ` lies in `𝓘(V) ⁿ⁺¹ Γ(M, V)`; the factorization is then
`AlgebraicGeometry.factorThruOfLocalMem`, and right cancellation against the monomorphism
`𝓘 ⁿ M ⟶ M` turns it into the factorization through the inclusion `𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹ M ⟶ 𝓘 ⁿ M` whose
cokernel the graded piece is.

**Right exactness is used in the left variable and conjugated by the braiding.** The cokernel
presentation `𝓘 ⁿ ⊗ (M / 𝓘 M) = coker (𝓘 ⁿ ⊗ 𝓘 M ⟶ 𝓘 ⁿ ⊗ M)` is right exactness of the tensor
product in the *right* variable, and the tree's public form of Tag 01CC
(`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.tensorSheafMap_exact` and `tensorSheafMap_epi`) is stated in
the left variable; its mirror image inside
`StacksFrontier/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/TensorPresentations.lean` is `private`. Rather than
restate that mirror, the whole descent is carried out on the swapped side, where the public
lemmas apply verbatim, and transported back along
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorPresentations.tensorSheafSwap` at the two ends only — once for the
map out of `M ⊗ 𝓘 ⁿ` and once for the resulting map out of `(M / 𝓘 M) ⊗ 𝓘 ⁿ`. The only fact
needed about the braiding is its naturality, which is public.

**`rw` is unusable on these composites, so every manipulation is a lemma whose ingredients are
all variables.** `X.Modules` is a `def` for `SheafOfModules X.ringCatSheaf`, and the tensor
product of Tag 01CA is indexed by `structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace`; the two spell the site
and the sheaf of rings differently, so a composite mixing a `sheafTensor` map with a morphism
declared in `X.Modules` is not type-correct at the `implicit` transparency `rw` uses to build its
motive — `rw [Category.assoc]` on `(pR ≫ idealPowTensorToSmul) ≫ ι` fails with an application
type mismatch on `X.ringCatSheaf`. Every reassociation and cancellation is therefore done once
and for all in an abstract category, with the composites, the morphisms and the equations between
them taken as variables (`Stacks.Abelian.assoc_eq_of_comp_eq`,
`comp_comp_eq_zero_of_comp_eq`, `eq_comp_of_comp_eq_of_mono`), and applied in term mode, where
only a definitional check is needed. This is the device of
`Stacks.Abelian.shortExact_of_cokernel_desc` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalFunctions/AdicGradedPieceShortExact.lean`, for the same
failure mode.

**Type ascription discharges the spelling mismatch once.** The same trick in its cheapest form:
`idealPowTensorToSmul_ι` is stated against `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPower`'s `𝓘 ⁿ M` while
`Stacks.Algebraization.submoduleInclusion_comp_ι` is stated against
`Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerMultiple`, and the two cannot both be matched by `rw`. Supplying
each as a `have` whose *stated* type uses the spelling the next step wants makes the elaborator
check the definitional equality once, after which nothing has to unify.

**Instance arguments are passed positionally.** `Epi`, like `Category`, is keyed on the ambient
category, so an `Epi` hypothesis proved at the `X.Modules` spelling is not found by instance
search for a lemma stated at the `SheafOfModules (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace)` spelling.
`epi_idealPowTensorQuotientToGradedPiece` and the two applications of Tag 01CC therefore pass
their `Epi` witness by position with `@`, forcing unification from its type, as
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Coherent/HomColimit/FirstDisplay.lean` does with `asIso`. For the
same reason `inferInstanceAs` is never given a `_` for the morphism: with the morphism still a
metavariable the search is run against `Epi ?f` and fails.

**`tensorModules` is ambiguous in the tree and is pinned by the `open` below.** Every occurrence
of it here is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealProduct.tensorModules`, the tensor product of
[Stacks, Tag 01CA] typed as an object of `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules`; at least a dozen
other declarations in the tree carry the same short name, several of them for the same
mathematical object at a different spelling. It is spelled short only because the fully qualified
name does not fit the line limit in the statements below.

**The two `idealPowerMultiple` constants.** `algebraization_idealPowerMultiple_eq` records that
`Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerMultiple` and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPower.idealPowerMultiple` are definitionally equal; see its
docstring, which also records which of the two the existing comparison lemmas are stated
against.

No `@[stacks]` attribute: Tag 0EXD asserts that
`AlgebraicGeometry.twoGeneratorFrobeniusColimitComparison` is an equivalence, and this is one
step inside the essential-surjectivity half of it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EXD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EXD)
